            <ArticleTitle>Pressure dependent release of atrial natriuretic peptide (ANP) in patients with chronic cardiac diseases: does it reset?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In patients with chronic cardiac disease plasma concentrations of atrial natriuretic peptide are elevated. The close relationships obtained between right (and/or left) atrial pressure and the peptide concentrations suggest a non-resetting phenomenon of the pressure induced release mechanism in the presence of a maintained responsiveness to acute stimuli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
